{"t": 1794105710.74135, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "Checkout paging \u2014 root cause found and fixed in code (pending deploy)\n\n\u2022 Alert: AG-7731 [FIRING] PaymentGatewayErrors checkout \u2014 gateway 4xx rate 38% since 07:41 UTC.\n\u2022 Cause: payment gateway switched to API 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"), which requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents). checkout/gateway.py still sent a float in euros, so every charge was rejected 400 `invalid_amount` (e.g. got 12.34).\n\u2022 Fix: checkout/gateway.py `charge_payload` now converts EUR to integer cents (12.34 -> 1234) with Decimal half-up rounding, keeping field name `amount` and currency EUR.\n\u2022 Verified locally: 12.34/0.01/19.99/100.00/0.30 all serialize as integer cents.\n\u2022 Next: deploy checkout and watch gateway 4xx rate / AG-7731 until it resolves. No other services appear affected."}, "ok": true}
